:"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":766},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820},{"base":"H0425","lemma":"אֵלָה","tr":"e·lah","gloss":"Elah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H1954","lemma":"הוֹשֵׁעַ","tr":"ho·she·a","gloss":"Hoshea","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H3807","lemma":"כָּתַת","tr":"ka·tat","gloss":"to crush","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":10,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"You are to fear the LORD your God and serve Him. Hold fast to Him and take your oaths in His name.","from":6},{"book":"JOS","chapter":23,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Instead, you shall hold fast to the LORD your God, as you have done to this day.","from":6},{"book":"2KI","chapter":23,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Neither before nor after Josiah was there any king like him, who turned to the LORD with all his heart and with all his soul and with all his strength, according to all the Law of Moses.","from":5},{"book":"2KI","chapter":19,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“Give this message to Hezekiah king of Judah: ‘Do not let your God, in whom you trust, deceive you by saying that Jerusalem will not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.","from":5},{"book":"2KI","chapter":16,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria, saying, “I am your servant and your son. Come up and save me from the hands of the kings of Aram and Israel, who are rising up against me.”","from":7},{"book":"2CH","chapter":31,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"When all this had ended, the Israelites in attendance went out to the cities of Judah and broke up the sacred pillars, chopped down the Asherah poles, and tore down the high places and altars throughout Judah and Benjamin, as well as in Ephraim and Manasseh, until they had utterly destroyed them all. Then all the Israelites returned to their cities, each to his own property.","from":4},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"If you love Me, you will keep My commandments.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":39,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And the Lordwas with Joseph, and he became a successful man, serving in the household of his Egyptian master.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":3},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"9-16":{"people":[{"id":"hezekiah-h2396g","name":"Hezekiah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":6,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"hoshea-h1954g","name":"Hoshea","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"elah-h0425i","name":"Elah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Hoshea","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"shalmaneser-h8022","name":"Shalmaneser","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"sennacherib-h5576","name":"Sennacherib","kind":"person","brief":"Emperor of Assyria","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":5,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"gozan-h1470","name":"Gozan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"habor-h2249","name":"Habor","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"halah-h2477","name":"Halah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"media-h4074h","name":"Media","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"lachish-h3923","name":"Lachish","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"H2396","lemma":"חִזְקִיָּהוּ","tr":"chiz·qiy·yah","gloss":"Hezekiah","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":127},{"base":"H0804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","tr":"ash·shur","gloss":"Assyria","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":151},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":877},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":820},{"base":"H1954","lemma":"הוֹשֵׁעַ","tr":"ho·she·a","gloss":"Hoshea","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H3603","lemma":"כִּכָּר","tr":"kik·kar","gloss":"Plain (of Jericho)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":68},{"base":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","tr":"sho·me·ron","gloss":"Samaria","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"H8022","lemma":"שַׁלְמַנְאֶ֫סֶר","tr":"shal·man·e·ser","gloss":"Shalmaneser","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3701","lemma":"כֶּ֫סֶף","tr":"ke·seph","gloss":"silver: money","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":403}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So Asa withdrew all the silver and gold that remained in the treasuries of the house of the LORD and the royal palace. He entrusted it to his servants and sent them with this message to Ben-hadad son of Tabrimmon, the son of Hezion, the king of Aram, who was ruling in Damascus:","from":15},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"“Let there be a treaty between me and you as there was between my father and your father. See, I have sent you a gift of silver and gold. Now go and break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, so that he will withdraw from me.”","from":15},{"book":"2KI","chapter":16,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Ahaz also took the silver and gold found in the house of the LORD and in the treasuries of the kingʼs palace, and he sent it as a gift to the king of Assyria.","from":15},{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But this is not so with My servant Moses; he is faithful in all My house.","from":12},{"book":"DEU","chapter":8,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Like the nations that the LORD has destroyed before you, so you will perish if you do not obey the LORD your God.","from":12},{"book":"DEU","chapter":11,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"but a curse if you disobey the commandments of the LORD your God and turn aside from the path I command you today by following other gods, which you have not known.","from":12},{"book":"DEU","chapter":29,"verse":24,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So all the nations will ask, ‘Why has the LORD done such a thing to this land? Why this great outburst of anger?’ And the people will answer, ‘It is because they abandoned the covenant of the LORD, the God of their fathers, which He made with them when He brought them out of the land of Egypt. They went and served other gods, and they worshiped gods they had not known—gods that the LORD had not given to them. Therefore the anger of the LORD burned against this land, and He brought upon it every curse written in this book. The LORD uprooted them from their land in His anger, rage, and great wrath, and He cast them into another land, where they are today.’","from":12},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"On that day My anger will burn against them, and I will abandon them and hide My face from them, so that they will be consumed, and many troubles and afflictions will befall them. On that day they will say, ‘Have not these disasters come upon us because our God is no longer with us?’","from":12}],"notes":[{"id":"mic-1-samaria","title":"Samaria made a heap in the field","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"17-25":{"people":[{"id":"hezekiah-h2396g","name":"Hezekiah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"rabshakeh-h7262","name":"Rabshakeh","kind":"person","brief":"Babylonian official","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"rab-saris-h7249g","name":"Rab-saris","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"tartan-h8661","name":"Tartan","kind":"person","brief":"Title of a leader","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"asaph-h0623h","name":"Asaph","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Joah","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"eliakim-h0471g","name":"Eliakim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hilkiah","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"hilkiah-h2518g","name":"Hilkiah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Eliakim","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"joah-h3098g","name":"Joah","kind":"person","brief":"K. Hezekiah's official","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"shebna-h7644","name":"Shebna","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547l","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":22}],"places":[{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"lachish-h3923","name":"Lachish","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"washer-s-field-h3526g","name":"Washer's Field","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"H0982","lemma":"בָּטַח","tr":"ba·tach","gloss":"to trust","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":120},{"base":"H7262","lemma":"רַבְשָׁקֵה","tr":"rav·sha·qeh","gloss":"Rabshakeh","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":32},{"base":"H6258","lemma":"עַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"now","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":433},{"base":"H2396","lemma":"חִזְקִיָּהוּ","tr":"chiz·qiy·yah","gloss":"Hezekiah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":127},{"base":"H7249","lemma":"רַב־סָרִיס","tr":"rav-sa·ris","gloss":"Rab-saris","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":643},{"base":"H0804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","tr":"ash·shur","gloss":"Assyria","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":151},{"base":"H9031","lemma":"ךָּ","tr":"ka","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":727},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":889},{"base":"H2088","lemma":"זֶה","tr":"zeh","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1176}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":20,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, along with all his might and how he constructed the pool and the tunnel to bring water into the city, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Judah?","from":17},{"book":"ISA","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD said to Isaiah, “Go out with your son Shear-jashub to meet Ahaz at the end of the aqueduct that feeds the upper pool, on the road to the Laundererʼs Field,","from":17},{"book":"ISA","chapter":20,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Before the year that the chief commander, sent by Sargon king of Assyria, came to Ashdod and attacked and captured it,","from":17},{"book":"ISA","chapter":30,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Egyptʼs help is futile and empty; therefore I have called her Rahab Who Sits Still.","from":21},{"book":"DEU","chapter":17,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But the king must not acquire many horses for himself or send the people back to Egypt to acquire more horses, for the LORD has said, ‘You are never to go back that way again.’","from":24},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When the Philistine looked and saw David, he despised him because he was just a boy, ruddy and handsome.","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Come here,” he called to David, “and I will give your flesh to the birds of the air and the beasts of the field!”","from":23},{"book":"2SA","chapter":8,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Joab son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder;","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"26-37":{"people":[{"id":"rabshakeh-h7262","name":"Rabshakeh","kind":"person","brief":"Babylonian official","count":4,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"eliakim-h0471g","name":"Eliakim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hilkiah","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"hilkiah-h2518g","name":"Hilkiah","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Eliakim","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"joah-h3098g","name":"Joah","kind":"person","brief":"K. Hezekiah's official","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"shebna-h7644","name":"Shebna","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"hezekiah-h2396g","name":"Hezekiah","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"asaph-h0623h","name":"Asaph","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Joah","count":1,"firstVerse":37}],"places":[{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"arpad-h0774","name":"Arpad","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"hamath-h2574g","name":"Hamath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"hena-h2012","name":"Hena","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"ivvah-h5755","name":"Ivvah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"samaria-h8111","name":"Samaria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"sepharvaim-h5617","name":"Sepharvaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":35}],"words":[{"base":"H7262","lemma":"רַבְשָׁקֵה","tr":"rav·sha·qeh","gloss":"Rabshakeh","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":32},{"base":"H5337","lemma":"נָצַל","tr":"na·tsal","gloss":"to rescue","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":213},{"base":"H2396","lemma":"חִזְקִיָּהוּ","tr":"chiz·qiy·yah","gloss":"Hezekiah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":127},{"base":"H0804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","tr":"ash·shur","gloss":"Assyria","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":151},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":724},{"base":"H3066","lemma":"יְהוּדִית","tr":"ye·hu·dit","gloss":"Judahite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H7644","lemma":"שֶׁבְנָא","tr":"shev·na","gloss":"Shebna","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H3098","lemma":"יוֹאָח","tr":"yo·ach","gloss":"Joah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H0471","lemma":"אֶלְיָקִים","tr":"el·ya·qim","gloss":"Eliakim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1142}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":4,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Throughout the days of Solomon, Judah and Israel dwelt securely from Dan to Beersheba, each man under his own vine and his own fig tree.","from":31},{"book":"DEU","chapter":8,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For the LORD your God is bringing you into a good land, a land of brooks and fountains and springs that flow through the valleys and hills;","from":32},{"book":"DEU","chapter":8,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"a land where you will eat food without scarcity, where you will lack nothing; a land whose rocks are iron and whose hills are ready to be mined for copper.","from":32},{"book":"EZR","chapter":4,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And in the days of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his associates wrote a letter to Artaxerxes. It was written in Aramaic and then translated.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You are also to say, ‘Look, your servant Jacob is right behind us.’” For he thought, “I will appease Esau with the gift that is going before me. After that I can face him, and perhaps he will accept me.”","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Please accept my gift that was brought to you, because God has been gracious to me and I have all I need.” So Jacob pressed him until he accepted.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Reuben returned to the pit and saw that Joseph was not there, he tore his clothes,","from":37},{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Jacob tore his clothes, put sackcloth around his waist, and mourned for his son many days.","from":37}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}